//huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \\href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/43}{[S2]}.\n\n\\subsection{Short English statement}\nDoes there exist a universal constant $C$ such that a nucleus of charge $Z$ can bind at most $Z+C$ electrons in the full many-body Schrödinger theory?\n\n\\subsection{Sources}\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003220 (OWR-14751-004). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.\n\\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.\n\\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.\n\\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/43}.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\label{end:30003220}","definition_file":"attacks/open_problems/top_problems/definitions/30003220.tex","link":"https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OWR-14751-004","external_url":"https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OWR-14751-004","sources":[{"citation":"ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003220 (OWR-14751-004). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath"},{"citation":"Original problem formulation and mathematical context.","url":"https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/43"}],"status":"solved","status_statement":null,"status_qualification":null,"status_reviewed_at":null,"attacks":[{"model":"OpenAI","status":"solved","entry_kind":"external_claim","claimant":"OpenAI","openai":{"schema_version":1,"source_repo":"https://github.com/openai/math","source_commit":"adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a","release_date":"2026-10-06","match":"stronger","resolution":"proved","independently_reviewed":false,"second_pass":"agreed","families":[{"family":"263","title":"The ionization and generalized ionization conjectures","subject":"Mathematical physics","manuscripts":[{"title":"Uniform excess charge for Coulomb molecules and the outer radi